    "https://jobs.lssu.edu/jobs/2026-2027-ncaa-sports-technical-director": {
      "title": "2026-2027 NCAA Sports Technical Director -",
      "description": "2026-2027 NCAA Sports Technical Director - Home Human Resources Benefits About LSSU Applicant Login Kiosk mode 2026-2027 NCAA Sports Technical Director Administrative Professional Athletics Temporary Part Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: 2026-2027 NCAA Sports Technical Director VP Area: Athletics Department: Athletics Published Salary Range: $30.00/hr Job Summary/Basic Function: Lake Superior State University Athletics is seeking a skilled and detail-oriented NCAA Sports Technical Director. Reporting directly to the Assistant Athletic Director for Game Management, this position is responsible for overseeing live in-venue production elements, jumbotron operations, and multi-media technical aspects of home athletic contests directly from the press box or scorers' table. The Technical Director ensures a high-quality, professional, and engaging game-day environment for student-athletes and fans while maintaining strict compliance with NCAA regulations. Key Responsibilities Jumbotron & Video Board Operation: Direct and manage the live in-arena video board production, including switching internal camera feeds, executing instant replays, playing institutional or sponsor graphics, and coordinating in-game crowd entertainment elements. Technical Game Management: Oversee the setup, operation, and teardown of press box and scorers' table technical systems, ensuring seamless integration of the official game clock, shot clocks, statistical software displays, and public address audio systems. Crew Leadership: Supervise, train, and coordinate student game-day staff assigned to technical roles, including scoreboard operators, replay technicians, camera operators, and audio engineers. Game Management Collaboration: Partner closely with the Assistant Athletic Director for Game Management and sports information staff to execute the pre-game script, timing protocols, and promotional activities flawlessly. Troubleshooting & Maintenance: Perform pre-game 