    "https://jobs.lssu.edu/jobs/2026-2027-ncaa-sports-public-address-announcer": {
      "title": "Similar Jobs",
      "description": "2026-2027 NCAA Sports Public Address Announcer - Home Human Resources Benefits About LSSU Applicant Login Kiosk mode 2026-2027 NCAA Sports Public Address Announcer Administrative Professional Athletics Temporary Part Time Add to favorites View favorites Title: 2026-2027 NCAA Sports Public Address Announcer VP Area: Athletics Department: Athletics Published Salary Range: $25/hr Job Summary/Basic Function: Lake Superior State University Athletics is seeking an enthusiastic and professional Public Address Announcer to serve as the in-venue voice for Laker Hockey, Volleyball, and Men’s and Women’s Basketball home events. This key gameday role will deliver real-time information, energize the crowd, maintain a professional tone, and contribute to an exciting and welcoming game environment for fans, student-athletes, and visiting teams. Key Responsibilities: Serve as the official voice for LSSU home contests in Hockey (Taffy Abel Arena), Volleyball, and Men’s & Women’s Basketball (Bud Cooper Gymnasium). Provide accurate and engaging live play-by-play information such as player introductions, scoring updates, penalties, fouls, substitutions, and timeouts in accordance with NCAA and conference policies. Deliver promotional reads, sponsor announcements, marketing initiatives, safety messages, and other in-game scripts as provided by LSSU Athletics. Work in coordination with the game operations crew, athletic communications staff, scoreboard operators, music coordinators, and officials to ensure smooth and timely game flow. Maintain a professional demeanor and appropriate energy level aligned with the LSSU Athletics brand and fan experience expectations. Be prepared for and responsive to in-game changes such as lineup adjustments, special ceremonies, and emergency announcements. Attend and contribute to pre-game run-throughs and production meetings, when applicable. Minimum Qualifications: Prior public speaking, voiceover, or announcing experience preferred (experience in athletics setting is a plus). Clear and confident vocal delivery with strong pronunciation and diction. Ability to remain calm under pressure and adapt in a fast-paced, live environment. Strong knowledge of (or willingness to learn) the rules and terminology of hockey, volleyball, and basketball. Reliability, punctuality, and strong communication skills. Availability to work evenings, weekends, and holidays in alignment with LSSU Athletics' home event schedule. Preferred Qualifications: Familiarity with NCAA and CCHA/GLIAC rules and team rosters. Comfortable using a microphone and working with audio/technical equipment. Collaborative mindset and ability to work well with a game-day team. Passion for college athletics and representing LSSU in a positive and enthusiastic manner. Apply now! Similar Jobs Economics Adjunct Instructor - MBA Program College of Business, Engineering, Computer Science, & Mathematics Lake Superior State University (LSSU) is seeking a dedicated individual to develop and deliver course content for ECON 645 (Economics for Managers) as part of our Master of Business Administration Program. The course will be offered online using Moodle from October 19 to December 11, 2026.\n\nAs one of LSSU’s core values is excellence in teaching and learning, the successful candidate will contribute to the institution’s educational mission by prioritizing student-centered learning and fostering a welcoming and inclusive academic environment for all. We seek applicants who are passionate about meeting students where they are and guiding them toward success. LSSU is a student-focused institution known for small class sizes, engaged faculty, and real-world learning. Our academic programs emphasize experiential education, preparing students to lead and innovate in their fields. 26/27 Student Admissions Ambassador Admissions Admissions Student Ambassadors are a vital part of the recruitment of prospective students and are employed directly by the Ad