    "https://jobs.lssu.edu/jobs/director-of-athletic-development-sault-ste-marie-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Director of Athletic Development",
      "description": "Director of Athletic Development - Sault Ste Marie, Michigan, United States Home Human Resources Benefits About LSSU Applicant Login Kiosk mode Director of Athletic Development Sault Ste Marie, Michigan, United States Athletics Regular Full Time Add to favorites View favorites FUNCTION AND RESPONSIBILITY The Director of Athletic Development reports to the Vice President for Advancement and serves as the fundraising and alumni engagement officer for Athletics, with a primary emphasis on the Men's DI Hockey program and secondary support across all athletic teams. The position secures philanthropic support at all giving levels and builds a comprehensive hockey alumni engagement program that connects former student-athletes to the program's history, current initiatives, and future direction. The role divides its focus between direct fundraising (70%) and strategic alumni engagement (30%), aligning efforts with overall fundraising strategy, donor management, and data management standards. The position works in collaboration with Athletic Administration to ensure that donor strategy, messaging, and alumni engagement activity align with Athletic priorities. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Manage an active portfolio of 100–150 prospects, qualifying, cultivating, soliciting, and closing major and principal gifts to meet annual and campaign fundraising goals in support of athletics, with a focus on the Men's DI Hockey program. Focuses on all gift levels with particular emphasis on major gifts of $5,000 and above, Guide each prospective donor through a deliberate progression of relationship-building, education, and solicitation, tailoring the approach and timing to the individual and moving each toward a gift in a disciplined, well-documented manner. Secure gifts in support of specific athletic and hockey priorities, including facilities projects, scholarships, program operations, and campaign initiatives, in coordination with Athletic Administration. Meet or exceed an established annual fundraising goal, and provide regular reports on prospect status and progress to the Vice President for Advancement. Identify, qualify, and cultivate new major gift prospects within the hockey alumni and broader athletics donor base, working to expand the overall pool of prospective donors. Develop strategic, personalized cultivation and stewardship plans for individual donors, and record all donor interactions, proposal stages, and portfolio activity in the Ellucian Banner database. Partner with Athletic Administration and the Advancement team to create compelling donor-facing proposals, case statements, and budget summaries for specific fundraising priorities. Coordinate with Advancement colleagues on planned giving and grant opportunities where they intersect with athletics prospects, referring and partnering as appropriate. Plan and execute donor engagement events, cultivation and solicitation visits, and support volunteer leadership groups or sport-specific boards, in coordination with Athletic Administration. Balance the solicitation of annual, often unrestricted gifts with the cultivation of larger gifts tied to specific strategic priorities, maintaining an appropriate pace of new donor acquisition alongside progress toward the overall fundraising goal. Develop and execute a comprehensive hockey alumni engagement strategy designed to strengthen lifelong connections between former student-athletes and the Laker Hockey program. Serve as the primary liaison to Laker Hockey alumni, maintaining regular communication through newsletters, digital content, personal outreach, milestone recognition, and alumni-focused initiatives including the Ring of Honor. Coordinate and host hockey alumni engagement activities, including home game hospitality, alumni weekends, reunions, networking events, championship anniversary celebrations, and special recognition programs. Work with Athletic Communications to collect, preserve, and share Laker Hockey history through feature stories, alumni spotlights, historical content, oral histories, and program archives. Build and maintain a comprehensive hockey alumni database, ensuring accurate records of career achievements, contact information, family milestones, and engagement history to support personalized outreach. Facilitate mentorship and networking opportunities between alumni and current student-athletes, and coordinate with Athletic Administration on alumni involvement in recruiting visits, program traditions, and student-athlete development programming. Acquire, maintain, and apply essential knowledge, skills, and abilities related to subject matter mastery of the job. Other duties as assigned. CORE COMPETENCIES To perform the job successfully, an individual should demonstrate the following competencies to perform the essential functions of this position. Customer Service: Listen and respond effectively to donor and alumni inquiries, resolve concerns to their satisfaction, and follow up consistently. Problem Solving: Identify and resolve challenges in donor cultivation and alumni engagement in a timely manner, gathering and analyzing information skillfully. Interpersonal Skills: Maintain confidentiality, remain open to new ideas, and build authentic relationships across the hockey alumni community and donor base. Oral Communication: Speak clearly and persuasively in a range of settings, and present philanthropic asks and program updates with confidence. Written Communication: Produce polished donor communications, proposals, and alumni content, and interpret and present data effectively. Planning and Organizing: Prioritize and plan cultivation, solicitation, and alumni engagement activity, and develop realistic action plans against fundraising goals. Quality Control: Maintain accuracy and thoroughness in donor records and portfolio management, and monitor own work to ensure data integrity. Adaptability: Adjust to shifting donor priorities, event schedules, and program needs, including evenings, weekends, and travel. Dependability: Maintain consistent attendance and availability for games and donor events, and respond to direction from Athletic Administration. Innovation/Initiative: Identify new alumni engagement and fundraising opportunities, and act on emerging priorities while maintaining focus on established goals. Apply now! Similar Jobs Economics Adjunct Instructor - MBA Program College of Business, Engineering, Computer Science, & Mathematics Lake Superior State University (LSSU) is seeking a dedicated individual to develop and deliver course content for ECON 645 (Economics for Managers) as part of our Master of Business Administration Program. The course will be offered online using Moodle from October 19 to December 11, 2026.\n\nAs one of LSSU’s core values is excellence in teaching and learning, the successful candidate will contribute to the institution’s educational mission by prioritizing student-centered learning and fostering a welcoming and inclusive academic environment for all. We seek applicants who are passionate about meeting students where they are and guiding them toward success. LSSU is a student-focused institution known for small class sizes, engaged faculty, and real-world learning. Our academic programs emphasize experiential education, preparing students to lead and innovate in their fields. 26/27 Student Admissions Ambassador Admissions Admissions Student Ambassadors are a vital part of the recruitment of prospective students and are employed directly by the Admissions Office at Lake Superior State University. Student Ambassadors are a select group of students dedicated to the positive promotion of the Institution and are an essential component of LSSU’s public relation and outreach.\n-Provide prospective students and their families with exceptional customer service\n-Build relationships and lend guidance to prospective students and their parents in person and over the telephone.\n-Provide information concerning Lake Superior State University and share positive LSSU related experiences with the students and families\n-Relay the prospective student’s needs and requests to the appropriate Admissions staff\n-Aim to encourage enrollment of prospective students\n-Participate in required training meetings and remain informed of current LSSU Admissions and campus life procedures, activities, andevents\n-Provide assistance in various events and programs planned by the Admissions Office such as GLSW, Orientation, and Open Houses\n-Give tours of campus to prospective students and their families\n-Perform other admissions related tasks as needed such as data input, mailings, answering multi-line phone, ETC\nSome weekend work opportunities. 2026-2027 Game Operations Student Staff Lake Superior State University Athletics is seeking dependable and enthusiastic students to join the Game Day Operations Team. These essential roles support the execution of home athletic events for Laker Hockey, Volleyball, and Men’s and Women’s Basketball, ensuring a professional and entertaining experience for student-athletes, fans, and visitors.\nKey Responsibilities:\nStudents may be assigned one or more of the following roles depending on availability, experience, and interest:\n1. Scoreboard & Time Clock Operator\nOperate the game clock, scoreboard, shot clock, and penalty timers using official systems, Work closely with officials and scorekeepers to ensure accurate timing and display, Maintain focus and attention to detail throughout the game.\n\n2. Technical Assistant\nAssist with technical aspects including lighting, jumbotron operation and sound support\n\n5. On-Ice / On-Court Support\nSet up and tear down game equipment (e.g., nets, scorer’s tables, signage, warm-up areas).\n\nSupport intermission and timeout activities\n\nHelp with managing benches, locker room access, and team logistics. 2026-2027 AY CFRE Student Assistant Center for Freshwater Research and Education This position will assist the CFRE leadership team with various administrative tasks and facility management. This position will also assist in driving the CFRE shuttle. They will assist with daily operations such as mail collection/distribution, assist with building maintenance, landscaping, basic cleaning/organization, and snow removal, assist with inventory management, lab set up and clean up, and driving the shuttle Student Worker - Registrar's Office Registrar Assist dept. with general office duties: file, run errands, handle mail, computer data entry and word processing. Applicant should be detail oriented, have strong communication and customer service skills. Students that are federal work study eligible are preferred. Scorekeeper - ACHA MD2, WD1 & WD2 Club Sports Scorekeeper for all ACHA D2 men's and ACHA DI women's hockey games played at Lake Superior State University. Some exceptions may apply to off campus games played at the Big Bear Arena or Pullar Stadium. Position requires availability most weekends throughout the hockey season. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 9e049271 Last Name (required) c1e985d1 Email (required) 3f7f962f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Lake Superior State University (LSSU) is an equal opportunity employer and complies with all applicable laws prohibiting discrimination on such factors as race, color, national origin, gender, religion, height, weight, familial status, marital status, veteran status, disability/handicap, age or sexual orientation in employment, or the provision of services, and provides upon request, reasonable accommodation including auxiliary aids and services necessary to afford individuals with disabilities an equal opportunity to participate in all programs and activities. Persons having Civil Rights inquiries may contact the Equal Opportunity Office at (906) 635-2213. Quick Links About LSSU Academics Admissions Athletics Campus Life Campus Map Traditions Copyright © 2022 All Rights Reserved by LSSU . Equal Opportunity | Diversity | Accessibility | Clery Act | Consumer Information | Campus Safety Information Candidate Details"
